      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "@{58c6b3cc227a56787575ebb4|full_name}: Yes. Even i7's struggle to run the game since it's not optimized in any way, still being an Early-Access title on Steam, but with multi-core performance getting faster and faster, it might be time for VRChat's devs to try switching to a new engine or figure out how to implement multi-core processing, which might help offload the loading and calculation issues by dumping them onto least/un-used cores.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-02-17T08:28:58.587Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Hello,\n\nI just recently got a Ryzen 5 1600 and was able to finally build my dream computer. I've noticed one issue, VRChat runs poorly on Ryzen chipsets cause of the lack of single-core performance. I've heard that VRChat is more suited for single-core performance, which the Ryzen chips are not good at.\n\nWith the 2nd Gen Ryzen chips coming out later this year, why not focus on trying to make VRChat multi-core and not single-core? It'll make it more compatible towards all available CPU's on the market, and draw in more potential players.",
